From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: skip redundant DSC bind on every kickoff

Mainline dpu_encoder_prepare_for_kickoff() calls dpu_encoder_prep_dsc()
on every frame. That path rewrites DSC PPS, rebinds dsc0→pp0 / dsc1→pp1,
and sets CTL_FLUSH bit 22 (pending_flush_dsc). On Xiaomi dagu L81A
(SM8250, 1600×2560@120 dual-DSC) the mux rewrite stalls wait_event on
CTL_FLUSH 107-219 ms (pending always 0x4218c0). DRM debug shows
"Binding dsc:0 to pp:0" / "Binding dsc:1 to pp:1" on every atomic.

Keep DSC enabled. Bind once at enable / hw_reset / runtime resume;
later kickoffs leave the mux. Disable still unpreps.

Applied by linux-mainline/scripts/apply-overlays.sh
(marker: dagu: skip redundant DSC prep).

Do not flash until head.S is checked (DAGU_PRIMARY_ENTRY_PROBE=0).

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 0000000..dagu0006 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -215,6 +215,11 @@ struct dpu_encoder_virt {
 
 	/* DSC configuration */
 	struct drm_dsc_config *dsc;
+	/* dagu: skip redundant DSC prep. Mainline rebinds DSC and
+	 * pending_flush_dsc (CTL bit 22) on every kickoff. L81A 120 Hz
+	 * dual-DSC then stalls CTL_FLUSH wait_event 107-219 ms.
+	 */
+	bool dsc_prepared;
 };
 
 #define to_dpu_encoder_virt(x) container_of(x, struct dpu_encoder_virt, base)
